# Implementation Plan — Journal Template System & Output Review (v3 Alignment)

This plan details the steps required to implement the remaining parts of the **Journal Template System — Implementation Plan v3**. We will build the Output Review step, the backend inline-edit endpoint, and the tabbed editor interface.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The PDF analyzer, journal settings registry, style-driven LaTeX generator, and journal profile onboarding page are already implemented and fully operational.
> We are now implementing the **Output Review** flow, which allows editors to edit block content *after* typesetting and see the changes updated in a live PDF preview instantly.

---

## Proposed Changes

We will implement the remaining requirements in the following sequence:

### 1. Backend Endpoint for Live Output Review Edits

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/sutra-engine/sutra/web/app.py)
- **New Endpoint**: `POST /project/{project_id}/review-edit`
  - Accepts a JSON payload containing updated blocks (e.g., edited text content, corrected heading levels, updated captions).
  - Loads the encrypted project state, updates the blocks list, runs block-level triage (to update warnings), and saves the state.
  - Re-runs the compilation pipeline (generating JATS XML and compiling the LaTeX PDF using Tectonic).
  - Returns `success: True`, the new `run_id`, and updated schema/compile logs.

### 2. Frontend Layout Restructuring

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/sutra-engine/sutra/web/templates/index.html)
- **Tabbed Workspace UI**:
  - Add workspace tab buttons in the project workspace area:
    - **Tab 1: Manuscript Tag Editor** (Step 1 — Block-level retagging and verification before compilation).
    - **Tab 2: Output Typeset Review** (Step 2 — Side-by-side typeset PDF and inline text editor for final polish).
  - Move the **Journal Profile Onboarding UI** out of the hidden dashboard section and make it easily accessible. We will structure it as a standalone section on the main dashboard to keep onboarding separate from individual article workspaces.
- **Tab 2 Layout**:
  - A split layout container:
    - **Left column**: PDF preview iframe displaying the live compiled PDF.
    - **Right column**: Output editor panel displaying scrollable, editable cards for every block (with its `% sutra-id:` comment reference).
  - Action buttons: "Regenerate Preview" (triggers live edit + compile) and "Finalize & Download Output" (gatelocks changes and downloads the final package ZIP).

### 3. Frontend Interactive Behavior

#### [MODIFY] [main.js](file:///c:/xampp/htdocs/sutra-engine/sutra/web/static/js/main.js)
- **Tab Switching**: Handle tab toggling between the Tag Editor (Tab 1) and Output Review (Tab 2).
- **Tab 2 Render Logic**:
  - Render each block of the document in editable input boxes/textareas.
  - Track edited blocks dynamically and apply a CSS highlight class (e.g., `.edited-block` with a subtle yellow background) to show unsaved/modified content.
  - When the "Regenerate" button is clicked:
    - Gather all text/tag modifications from the editable cards.
    - Send them to `/project/{project_id}/review-edit`.
    - Reload the PDF preview iframe src with the new `run_id`.
    - Refresh block states and clear the unsaved highlights once the new compilation succeeds.

